llm_response:
The `:has-text("Playwright")` selector matches many elements, including the `<body>` tag, because it finds every element on the page that contains the specified text.

To narrow this to the specific element you want, you should use a more specific locator that identifies the container of the text. The documentation recommends prefixing the selector with the specific element type that contains the text. For example:

```javascript
// Correct, only matches the <article> element
await page.locator('article:has-text("Playwright")').click();
```

If you have multiple similar elements and need to select a specific one, you can use `:nth-match()`:

```javascript
// Selects the third occurrence
await page.locator(':nth-match(:has-text("Playwright"), 3)').click();
```

While you can also use `locator.first()`, `locator.last()`, or `locator.nth()`, these are not recommended because they may target the wrong element if the page structure changes. The preferred approach is to create a locator that uniquely identifies the target element.

