To achieve this behavior, use the `reuseExistingServer` property within the `webServer` object in your `playwright.config.ts` file, set to `!process.env.CI`.

This configuration ensures that Playwright will reuse an existing server locally (when `process.env.CI` is undefined) but will not reuse an existing server on CI (where `process.env.CI` is typically set), forcing it to start a fresh server.

Example configuration:

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';

export default defineConfig({
  webServer: {
    command: 'npm run start',
    url: 'http://localhost:3000',
    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,
  },
});
```

